<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meskwaki</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fox people, Mesquakie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Meskwaki, called the Fox by the French, are an Algonquian-speaking Indigenous people of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a>, closely related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sauk">Sauk</a>. In the early 18th century they fought the Fox Wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and its Indigenous allies, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, which cost them heavily. Allied with the Sauk, they later moved west, and their descendants form the Meskwaki Nation in Iowa and belong to the Sac and Fox nations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meskwaki.jpg" alt="Meskwaki" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Bird King, Lithograph by J.T. Bowen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kee-shes-wa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
